// LOOPS OF IMPORTS ARE REFUSED, each at the edge that closes it, and nothing
// else is reported.
//
// Imports form a DAG at every scale, sister modules as well as packages [Jon 23
// Sep]. The modules are put in dependency order before any name folds, and each
// loop is ErrorImportLoop, naming the modules round it, at the import or the
// 'extends' that closes it: two sisters importing each other, three round one
// ring, and a loop an 'extends' closes.
//
// The loops are not cut, and the fold passes still carry each re-export round
// them, pass after pass until one binds nothing new (modFoldAll). That is what
// this scenario pins beside the refusals: every name a body below reaches
// through a loop is bound, so the loop is the one thing reported and nothing it
// left half-folded is reported missing as well. Each case is one a single fold
// pass would have lost.
//
// The subfolders are drawn in sorted order and their folds start in that order,
// which is what decides who reads whom mid-fold, and which import closes each loop:
//   gamma/gamma.cone       the names re-exported: shared, more, Tone, Config; in
//                          no loop
//   alpha/alpha.cone       imports beta and bravo, THEN re-exports gamma's shared,
//                          Tone and Config
//   beta/beta.cone         imports alpha and folds from it by a listed clause, and
//                          folds Tone's variants through the path alpha.Tone
//   bravo/bravo.cone       a wildcard of alpha, and a global's fold and an enum's
//                          'use' naming bare what the wildcard has not brought yet
//   delta/delta.cone       the other order: delta folds first and reads epsilon
//   epsilon/epsilon.cone   imports delta, then re-exports gamma's shared
//   kappa/kappa.cone       imports lambda and relay, THEN re-exports gamma's more
//   lambda/lambda.cone     a wildcard 'pub use' of kappa: kappa -> lambda -> kappa
//   onward/onward.cone     a wildcard of lambda, one wildcard further on, in no loop
//   relay/relay.cone       folds more privately from gamma, and publicly from kappa
//                          round the loop kappa -> relay -> kappa
//   plinth/plinth.cone     imports tower with 'use *', THEN re-exports gamma's more
//   tower/tower.cone       extends plinth: a loop an 'extends' edge closes
//   tri1/tri1.cone         three modules round one loop, each carrying on the
//   tri2/tri2.cone           next one's names with 'pub use *': tri1 -> tri2 ->
//   tri3/tri3.cone           tri3 -> tri1, and tri1 re-exports gamma's shared too
//
// module-import-cycle-nameres holds what a loop still leaves missing, and a
// collision a loop brings.

fn reach() i64 {
  // A listed clause, one name under a local spelling, and Tone's variants
  // folded through a path naming alpha's re-export
  beta.b() + beta.tone()
  // bravo's global and its 'use' of Tone waited for alpha's Config and Tone
  + bravo.b()
  // The other order: delta folds first, so it reads epsilon complete
  + delta.d()
  // lambda's wildcard read kappa mid-fold, carried on by its 'pub use *',
  // reached by a path, and one wildcard further on
  + lambda.f() + lambda.more() + onward.g()
  // relay folded more privately from gamma, and publicly from kappa round the
  // loop: one binding, public
  + relay.more()
  // tower extends plinth, which imports tower
  + tower.more() + plinth.viaTower()
  // Three modules round one loop
  + tri3.two() + tri3.shared() + tri2.one();
}
